  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elbitamerica secured $358M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Elbitamerica recorded 178 awards for the period, with an average award size of $2M, and obligations are up 359.5% year over year. Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $306M to Elbitamerica in FY2026 to date. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market, accounting for $316M of FY2026 to date obligations. Department of Defense obligated $51.5M to Elbitamerica in the same period. Historical obligations show variation: Elbitamerica recorded $115M in FY21, $119M in FY22, $96.8M in FY23, $137M in FY24, and $77.9M in FY25, before the FY2026 to date total of $358M. Other NAICS markets with recorded FY2026 to date obligations include All Other Miscellaneous General Purpose Machinery Manufacturing at $14.4M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $10.9M. The current-year totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Elbitamerica's biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security is the largest buying agency, obligating $306M in FY2026 to date. Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer, obligating $51.5M. Department of Transportation recorded $0 in obligations for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive Elbitamerica's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing is the largest market, with $316M in FY2026 to date obligations. All Other Miscellaneous General Purpose Machinery Manufacturing and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing follow, with $14.4M and $10.9M respectively. Smaller recorded markets include Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $4.5M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $2.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
